\[\begin{array}{l}\mbox{$Y_{\nu}(ze^{\mathrm{i}\pi t})=e^{\mathrm{i}(t+1)\pi t}I_{ \nu}(z)-(2/\pi)e^{-\mathrm{i}\pi t}K_{\nu}(z)$}\\ \hskip 56.905512pt(-\pi<\!\arg z\!\leq\!\frac{1}{2}\pi)\\ \mbox{$9.6.6$}\hskip 34.143307ptI_{-n}(z)=I_{n}(z),K_{-\nu}(z)=K_{\nu}(z)\end{array}\]

Most of the properties of modified Bessel functions can be deduced immediately from those of ordinary Bessel functions by application of these relations.

### Limiting Forms for Small Arguments

When \(p\) is fixed and \(z\!\to\!0\)

\[\begin{array}{l}\mbox{$I_{\nu}(z)\sim(\frac{1}{2}z)^{\nu}/\Gamma(\nu+1)$} \hskip 14.226378pt(v\!\neq\!-1,-2,\ldots)\\ \mbox{$F_{\nu}(z)\sim-\ln z$}\\ \mbox{$F_{\nu}(z)\sim\frac{1}{2}(\frac{1}{2}z)^{-n}\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n-1} \frac{(n\!-\!k\!-\!1)!}{k!}\hskip 14.226378pt(-\frac{1}{4}z^{2})^{k}$}\\ \hskip 14.226378pt+(-)^{-n+1}\ln\,(\frac{1}{2}z)I_{n}(z)\\ \hskip 14.226378pt+(-)^{-n+1}\frac{1}{2}(\frac{1}{2}z)^{n}\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n }\,(\psi(k\!+\!1)+\psi(n\!+\!k\!+\!1))\,\frac{(\frac{1}{4}z^{2})^{k}}{k!(n\!+\! k)!}\end{array}\]

where \(\psi(n)\) is given by 6.3.2.

